1135:- `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts` only where its app-shell-facing persistence port shape must be narrowed or moved behind a typed adapter
1149:Current source evidence shows the remaining central problem moved into the application app-shell runtime/composition boundary, not into `App.vue` markup. `createAppShellRuntime` still constructs `World`, `CommandStack`, default `GoogleDriveService`, default `ProjectService`, browser `window.localStorage`, browser scheduler, and installs keyboard handling on `window` from the runtime (`frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:21`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:22`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:23`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:24`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:27`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:28`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:29`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:101`). `AppShellPorts` still exposes a persistence port typed directly in terms of `CommandStack`, `World`, and `ProjectData` from `ProjectService`, so app-session orchestration is not insulated from concrete command/domain/persistence shapes (`frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellPorts.ts:2`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellPorts.ts:3`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellPorts.ts:5`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellPorts.ts:24`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellPorts.ts:25`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellPorts.ts:27`).
1259:The next central canonical stage should be `cycle-022-fresh-scout-proposals-post-021-plan-correction` for **Wave 022 — Runtime session kernel and persistence port boundary**, subject to a fresh current-source scope check before any implementation. Wave 022 remains the highest-centrality next candidate because it addresses runtime/session ownership, project-session persistence ports, initialization/session lifecycle, and the raw `World`/`CommandStack` pair contract that later command-producer, persistence, rendering, backend, validation, placeholder/debug, and docs waves should consume rather than preserve.
1261:This re-rank does **not** authorize using Wave 021 to broaden into canvas movement/style, construction, process-history, panel/toolbar, command descriptor/replay, persistence schema, rendering, Three/canvas, backend/docs/specs, package/tooling, Drive/auth, validation-platform, or UI feature work. If the Wave 022 fresh scope check finds its premises already satisfied or invalidated by current source, edit this plan through another reviewed plan-correction mini-cycle before proceeding.
1281:## Wave 022 — Runtime session kernel and persistence port boundary
1307:The Wave 021 plan correction verifies that `SelectionUseCases` no longer owns delete command construction, while `SelectionDeletionCommandService` owns `new Command`, `DeletionSequenceFactory`, `commit()`, and `commandStack.push()` for that slice (`frontend/src/application/appShell/SelectionUseCases.ts:1-13`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/SelectionUseCases.ts:30-35`, `frontend/src/application/selectionDeletion/SelectionDeletionCommandService.ts:1-5`, `frontend/src/application/selectionDeletion/SelectionDeletionCommandService.ts:12-17`, `frontend/src/application/selectionDeletion/SelectionDeletionCommandService.ts:30-37`). Other direct command producers and broader app-shell/runtime ownership remain future candidates, but Wave 022 must verify its own premise from current source rather than relying on older Cycle 021 implementation artifacts.
1309:Current source evidence to verify in the next fresh scope check suggests the most central residual is not another selection/delete leaf producer first, but the runtime/session contract that may still leak concrete kernel state into persistence and session use cases. `createAppShellRuntime` imports and instantiates concrete `World` and `CommandStack` directly (`frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:2`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:3`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:17`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:18`) and wires those concrete objects into `SelectionDeletionCommandService` (`frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:40`). `AppShellPorts` defines the project-session persistence port in terms of concrete `CommandStack`, `World`, and `ProjectData` (`frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellPorts.ts:2`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellPorts.ts:3`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellPorts.ts:5`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellPorts.ts:26`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellPorts.ts:28`). The adapter then passes those objects straight to static `ProjectService` methods (`frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter.ts:1`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter.ts:2`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter.ts:3`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter.ts:7`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter.ts:8`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter.ts:15`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter.ts:16`). `ProjectService` itself is explicitly command-stream persistence orchestration and consumes `CommandStack`/`World` (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:2`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:5`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:6`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:27`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:45`).
1313:Other residual command producers remain real but are lower priority for Wave 022 because they are leaf use-case seams that should consume a cleaner runtime/session kernel once it exists: point movement (`frontend/src/application/canvas/CanvasPointMovementUseCase.ts:9`, `frontend/src/application/canvas/CanvasPointMovementUseCase.ts:12`, `frontend/src/application/canvas/CanvasPointMovementUseCase.ts:32`, `frontend/src/application/canvas/CanvasPointMovementUseCase.ts:33`), style updates (`frontend/src/application/canvas/CanvasStyleUseCase.ts:8`, `frontend/src/application/canvas/CanvasStyleUseCase.ts:11`, `frontend/src/application/canvas/CanvasStyleUseCase.ts:14`, `frontend/src/application/canvas/CanvasStyleUseCase.ts:15`), construction (`frontend/src/application/construction/ConstructionUseCases.ts:35`, `frontend/src/application/construction/ConstructionUseCases.ts:36`, `frontend/src/application/construction/ConstructionUseCases.ts:43`, `frontend/src/application/construction/ConstructionUseCases.ts:44`), and process-history edits (`frontend/src/application/processHistory/ProcessHistoryUseCases.ts:20`, `frontend/src/application/processHistory/ProcessHistoryUseCases.ts:22`, `frontend/src/application/processHistory/ProcessHistoryUseCases.ts:23`, `frontend/src/application/processHistory/ProcessHistoryUseCases.ts:73`, `frontend/src/application/processHistory/ProcessHistoryUseCases.ts:77`, `frontend/src/application/processHistory/ProcessHistoryUseCases.ts:78`). Canvas rendering still injects the concrete `World` and polls it for versions (`frontend/src/components/workspace/SvgCanvas.vue:412`, `frontend/src/components/workspace/SvgCanvas.vue:479`, `frontend/src/components/workspace/SvgCanvas.vue:480`), but rendering/domain-contract cleanup is less central than defining the session object those views observe.
1317:The app shell has an explicit runtime session boundary that owns the current in-memory `World`, `CommandStack`, initialization lifecycle, snapshot request, restore request, dirty/version implications, and command-history exposure needed by app-shell use cases. App-shell use cases and persistence ports should consume a named session/kernel interface rather than passing raw `{ world, commandStack }` pairs and `ProjectData` through broad ports.
1347:All Wave 022 validation stdout/stderr must be captured to stable files under the reviewed Cycle 022 implementation directory's `validation/` subdirectory. Undefined commands may be skipped only with exact package-script evidence in the implementation log; defined root or workspace commands are mandatory.
1368:Raw `World`/`CommandStack` pairs in app-shell persistence ports are internal architecture debt, not a public compatibility contract. Preserving both the old pair-based persistence calls and a named runtime-session boundary would keep the ownership model ambiguous and make later command-producer and persistence waves harder. Delete the old port shape and update active callers/tests directly once the reviewed boundary is selected.
1377:Added by `cycle-023-wave-plan-extension` after Wave 022 completed. Requires review of this plan extension before the canonical `cycle-023-fresh-scout-proposals` stage and before any implementation. This entry is grounded in current post-Wave-022 source evidence and the Wave 022 implementation/closure log, which explicitly marks Wave 022 complete while leaving raw `World`/`CommandStack` accessors for active-plane, keyboard/history, selection, command services, rendering-facing consumers, and adapter-private persistence casts as residual debt.
1393:This wave owns the consumer-facing seams left by Wave 022's new `RuntimeSession`: active-plane state, keyboard undo/redo history, selection read/delete support, and the adapter-private persistence handle. It must not migrate unrelated leaf command producers in canvas movement/style/construction/process-history, redesign command descriptors or persistence schema/replay, reopen Drive/auth/browser composition, alter rendering/presentation/domain realization/Three scene-host boundaries, change backend/docs/spec/package/tooling, or perform validation-platform/debug cleanup.
1399:Wave 022 completed the runtime-session kernel and narrowed the public app-shell persistence contract: `RuntimeSession` now owns the current `World`/`CommandStack` lifecycle, project/session/autosave use cases consume session methods, and `ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter` is the only app-shell bridge to `ProjectService` (`architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/implementation-log.md`, “Production files changed”; “DELETE list / proofs”; “Validation-and-preview closure — t1 independent verification”). The same log records residual risks that raw-object accessors remain for active-plane, keyboard/history, selection, rendering-facing consumers, and that `ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter` still uses private casts from opaque handles (`architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/implementation-log.md`, “Residual risks and next-wave candidates”; “Next-wave recommendation / re-rank”).
1421:- Delete `ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter` private casts from opaque runtime handles to `{ world, commandStack }` if a typed package-private adapter handle can preserve the Wave 022 public app-shell contract without schema/replay redesign.
1439:Depends on Wave 022 because that wave created `RuntimeSession` and intentionally left raw consumer accessors plus adapter-private casts as residual debt. It is ordered before leaf canvas/style/construction/process-history command-producer cleanup, backend/frontend contract stance, validation-gate hardening, placeholder/debug cleanup, docs/spec drift, and remaining rendering/domain-contract seams because those later waves should consume a stable runtime-session/command-history boundary rather than broad raw `World`/`CommandStack` access.
1832:Current source confirms the next central seam is no longer tool context but runtime read-model concentration. `RuntimeSession` privately owns `World` and `CommandStack` (`frontend/src/application/appShell/RuntimeSession.ts:37`, `:38`, `:39`) and then directly constructs canvas, process-tree, elements-panel, three-presentation, active-plane, selection, command-history, selection-deletion, and persistence ports (`frontend/src/application/appShell/RuntimeSession.ts:42-80`, `:83-160`, `:163-183`, `:186-242`, `:263-281`). `canvasViewPort()` still creates `CanvasWorldReadPort` and `ToolInteractionReadPort` from the private world and computes input transforms by iterating all projection planes (`frontend/src/application/appShell/RuntimeSession.ts:42-56`). `processTreeReadPort()` reads `world.getProcessTree()` and dependency service data while constructing panel DTOs (`frontend/src/application/appShell/RuntimeSession.ts:83-107`). `elementsPanelPort()` groups domain objects with concrete `instanceof` checks and directly mutates `visualStyle` plus `world.markDirty()` for visibility (`frontend/src/application/appShell/RuntimeSession.ts:110-160`).
